WEBVTT

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:10.610
I was doing precisely the same as always.

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:14.280
At that time, I was a new recruit at the hotel.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:18.350
As I recall, I was absorbed in my duties, and quite some time passed...

00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:21.350
...before I knew that some sort of dreadful incident had occurred.

00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:24.490
Huh? It was really a surprise.

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:28.450
When we returned from our vacation, the airport and even the roads had been closed off.

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:35.090
I was still a child, so it was like I was watching a movie or something.

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:39.100
I never imagined that even we would be engulfed by it.

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:50.970
As you know, it was mass confusion, and at any rate...

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:58.390
Sorry, the fact is, I don't remember well, probably because I was scared to death.

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:01.190
It's pathetic, but really, that time was...

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:05.260
Well, you know, I never even imagined it.

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:07.800
That our everyday routine, which we'd gone through again and again,

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:10.230
...would come to an end on that day, was just...

00:03:31.490 --> 00:03:36.530
Twin X, it occurred just after we had opened this hotel.

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:40.430
We opened this establishment up to its victims for a number of months.

00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:44.860
Now, even that is a memory filled with nostalgia.

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:56.110
Something you want to ask?

00:03:56.110 --> 00:04:01.020
Yes, uh... Why was it that you didn't tell me?

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:02.490
I mean...

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:05.720
That you know my dad.

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:11.390
I saw the picture, the one you're in with my dad.

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:17.100
It's because I thought there was no particular need to tell you.

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:24.810
Tell me, please. Tell me about my dad!

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:29.210
At this point, there's no use in your knowing such things, is there?

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:30.880
I just want to know.

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:34.090
Please, anything at all is fine.

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:36.220
What kind of person was he?

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:41.730
I don't know. Now, leave it at that and go back to your room.

00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:44.960
Then why did you take my sister and me in?

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:47.270
Because we're Terumichi Madoka's children?!

00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:47.530
Tatsuya!
Because we're Terumichi Madoka's children?!

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:48.460
Tatsuya!

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:55.700
I told you, didn't I? That I needed you two to fight against Gilgamesh?

00:04:56.910 --> 00:04:58.280
But...

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:03.510
Recall one more thing. You and Kiyoko were bought by me.

00:05:08.890 --> 00:05:12.980
You need to bear in mind your situation and become a bit more of an adult.

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:17.820
"Why?" "What?" "How come?" You should be ashamed.

00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:36.750
She didn't come.

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:40.180
It's because I asked her too much about too many things.

00:05:40.590 --> 00:05:43.750
She gets sulky really easily, that woman.

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:47.020
But that she was at Heaven's Gate is a real surprise.

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:51.260
Yeah, I think she knows a little more about my dad too.

00:05:51.730 --> 00:05:54.070
It'll probably be impossible to get anything out of her.

00:05:54.070 --> 00:05:56.330
It's that woman after all.

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:59.530
I kinda hate how you call her "that woman," Fu.

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:01.910
Why's that?

00:06:01.910 --> 00:06:05.340
No reason, really. Just something about it...

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:09.440
I get it. It's because you want to call her "Mama," right, Toru?

00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:11.350
No way!

00:06:14.250 --> 00:06:16.020
That's why you're still a little boy.

00:06:22.930 --> 00:06:24.190
Mitleid...

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:30.100
Heaven's Gate was that company's predecessor.

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:32.270
They may have some material on it.

00:06:32.270 --> 00:06:34.600
Really? What can we do to see them?

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:41.410
We can take it upon ourselves to look.

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:44.850
Let's go now.

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:48.250
Huh?! Is it normal to take things that far?

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:52.250
I didn't actually tell you to come along or anything, did I?

00:06:53.860 --> 00:06:57.390
So you want to know about the Countess that badly.

00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:00.820
Toru, how about you?

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:02.600
I'm...

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:04.360
You're gonna tattle to Mama, right?

00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:06.700
I'm going!

00:07:09.010 --> 00:07:10.530
Well then, we'll be back.

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:15.640
I didn't actually say I wasn't going, did I?

00:08:28.220 --> 00:08:30.190
There's nobody here, huh?

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:31.520
Don't let your guard down.

00:08:35.930 --> 00:08:39.120
<i>There should probably be something like a reference room.</i>

00:08:47.870 --> 00:08:50.400
<i>Fu, you can go home if you like.</i>

00:08:53.780 --> 00:08:55.410
I found it.

00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:08.760
Memorial State Museum, huh?

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:10.360
That's it, huh?

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:11.590
Let's go and see.

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:52.090
This is the place.

00:10:02.210 --> 00:10:04.240
Amazing, all this data!

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:15.760
Those are clones.

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:17.100
Clones?

00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:19.460
They could do things like that in the old days.

00:10:22.570 --> 00:10:24.130
Here we are.

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:32.810
So which one?

00:10:32.810 --> 00:10:34.610
These?

00:10:42.890 --> 00:10:44.190
There's too much!

00:10:44.190 --> 00:10:45.890
Let's do a computer data search.

00:10:45.890 --> 00:10:50.260
No good. It'll leave a record. We can just divide it up.

00:10:51.330 --> 00:10:55.830
If we go through and scan in the images, it won't take that much time.

00:10:55.830 --> 00:10:57.360
The images?

00:11:05.610 --> 00:11:11.410
Instead of reading, use Dynamis to go through and pick up the images made by the letters.

00:11:12.550 --> 00:11:15.020
We'll share the information later.

00:11:16.250 --> 00:11:17.450
Like this.

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:29.000
Get it?

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:30.970
Let's hurry.

00:11:30.970 --> 00:11:32.700
Are you serious?

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:34.100
I'm very serious.

00:11:37.110 --> 00:11:39.910
I guess I shouldn't have come after all.

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:54.730
Don't look at the letters.

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:58.660
If you gaze at it blankly, it'll come into focus with your Dynamis.

00:11:58.660 --> 00:12:00.390
So you say, but...

00:12:19.750 --> 00:12:24.590
<i>In the war that unfolded at the beginning of this century in the cradle of civilization,</i>

00:12:25.490 --> 00:12:27.860
<i>...Uruk became the site of the hardest fighting.</i>

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:30.390
<i>More than ten years after the war,</i>

00:12:30.390 --> 00:12:35.530
<i>...numerous paranormal phenomena are reported in this Mesopotamian city.</i>

00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:41.170
<i>An investigation resulted in the confirmation of an enormous ruin resting below the city.</i>

00:12:41.170 --> 00:12:43.300
<i>It was Gilgamesh's tomb.</i>

00:12:44.180 --> 00:12:46.080
Gilgamesh...

00:12:46.080 --> 00:12:50.840
<i>Gilgamesh, a legendary king, said to be part human, part god.</i>

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:55.950
<i>In the ruin existed an enormous cavern which gave access to a subspace.</i>

00:12:56.150 --> 00:12:59.420
<i>This was what was giving rise to the numerous paranormal phenomena.</i>

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:02.860
<i>The cavern was named Delphys,</i>

00:13:02.860 --> 00:13:06.190
<i>...and it became a zone of joint international control in its entirety.</i>

00:13:06.730 --> 00:13:11.540
<i>Around this base, distinguished scientists from all nations of the world were gathered,</i>

00:13:11.540 --> 00:13:14.410
<i>...and a gigantic research facility was established.</i>

00:13:14.410 --> 00:13:16.370
<i>That was Heaven's Gate.</i>

00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:20.550
<i>The Heaven's Gate research produced steady results,</i>

00:13:20.550 --> 00:13:23.780
<i>...and it was expected to have applications in many fields.</i>

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:26.080
<i>The curtain was about to be raised...</i>

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:30.580
<i>...on an era of revolutionary technologies that would overturn the common worldview.</i>

00:13:42.970 --> 00:13:45.530
Hey, something's coming.

00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:51.730
<i>Many dangers came with the research into the not-yet-understood space of Delphys.</i>

00:13:52.940 --> 00:13:54.980
<i>In an attempt to ensure the scientists' safety,</i>

00:13:54.980 --> 00:14:00.880
<i>...bodies such as Orga were set up within Heaven's Gate. Orga was...</i>

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:08.030
This is strange. I can't tell what it is that's approaching.

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:12.330
Hey, do you know what "Orga" is? I can't get an image of it.

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:13.560
Orga?

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:17.530
Hey, Isamu...

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:22.630
I seem to remember, hasn't the Countess called you and the others that, Fujisaki?

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:24.270
Did she?

00:14:25.610 --> 00:14:26.940
Hey!

00:14:28.610 --> 00:14:29.980
They're here!

00:14:45.160 --> 00:14:47.000
What are these? Are they alive?

00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:52.100
No, they're robots, moved by electronic brains. This can't be...

00:14:52.100 --> 00:14:53.830
There's the Sheltering Sky, right?

00:14:55.510 --> 00:14:56.940
But then, what are these?

00:15:00.340 --> 00:15:02.010
They're creepy somehow.

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:25.100
They're targeting Madoka!

00:15:25.100 --> 00:15:26.360
How come?!

00:15:32.540 --> 00:15:35.810
Toru, what are you chickening out for? They're just machines, right?

00:15:35.810 --> 00:15:36.950
No they're not.

00:15:36.950 --> 00:15:38.680
They are, I'm telling you!

00:15:49.360 --> 00:15:50.830
What...

00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:36.270
Toru!

00:16:52.790 --> 00:16:54.160
Orga?

00:17:00.430 --> 00:17:01.900
Oh! The books are...

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:17.810
Whether or not we leave a computer record is a moot point now, isn't it?

00:17:23.650 --> 00:17:26.320
The only things here are official references,

00:17:26.320 --> 00:17:28.830
...so they probably didn't find out anything significant, but...

00:17:28.830 --> 00:17:30.260
You've got your hands full too, don't you?

00:17:31.660 --> 00:17:35.000
I gave those children a sound punishment for it.

00:17:37.430 --> 00:17:39.730
When will you tell them the truth?

00:17:40.740 --> 00:17:42.570
When they find out, they'll likely be bitter.

00:17:47.910 --> 00:17:50.510
That may be, but these robots...

00:17:52.520 --> 00:17:57.180
You've become capable of quite inhuman things too, haven't you?

00:18:00.560 --> 00:18:01.960
If you'll excuse me.

00:18:03.530 --> 00:18:06.760
Wait, my calling you was about a different matter.

00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:12.870
It's about Tatsuya Madoka.

00:18:16.110 --> 00:18:20.010
You're aware that our corporation recently made him an ID card.

00:18:20.010 --> 00:18:21.500
It's about the data from that.

00:18:27.420 --> 00:18:28.850
Is this...

00:18:33.760 --> 00:18:35.190
It can't be...

00:18:36.330 --> 00:18:39.160
We really upset the Countess, didn't we?

00:18:39.160 --> 00:18:41.700
Probably because she's got a guilty conscience,

00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:44.340
...like something she doesn't want us to know.

00:18:44.340 --> 00:18:46.060
Not necessarily.

00:18:49.270 --> 00:18:53.410
It could also be that she doesn't want to worry us needlessly,

00:18:53.410 --> 00:18:55.780
...since she is the type that keeps burdens to herself.

00:18:56.310 --> 00:18:57.750
Wow...

00:18:57.750 --> 00:18:59.150
What?

00:18:59.150 --> 00:19:01.080
You are serious about her after all.

00:19:02.450 --> 00:19:05.750
When you were with me, you never backed me up like that.

00:19:06.420 --> 00:19:08.390
I'm getting all jealous.

00:19:08.390 --> 00:19:09.920
Fu!

00:19:10.260 --> 00:19:11.820
I'm kidding.

00:19:13.300 --> 00:19:15.360
But I just went to the trouble of changing that!

00:19:16.270 --> 00:19:20.170
I'm sorry, but I ask that you redo everything.

00:19:20.540 --> 00:19:23.840
We can't possibly admit guests in this state.

00:19:23.840 --> 00:19:24.940
Are you for real?

00:19:24.940 --> 00:19:28.240
We make every effort to provide perfect service.

00:19:29.150 --> 00:19:31.270
And if you could watch your choice of words as well...

00:19:46.760 --> 00:19:49.670
Oh! Excuse me!

00:19:58.480 --> 00:20:00.070
I'm sorry.

00:20:01.810 --> 00:20:04.910
He was fond of music.

00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:11.680
He was a superb scientist, and was also wonderful as a human being.

00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:56.170
<i>We have the patient's registration in the backup files.</i>

00:20:56.170 --> 00:21:01.870
<i>Her registration number is N108894. Name: Hiroko Kageyama.</i>

00:21:10.680 --> 00:21:15.180
Your father changed absolutely everything with Twin X.

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:21.320
He even changed himself into a new human being named Enkidu.

00:21:28.970 --> 00:21:33.430
He will likely have to pay the price for it though.

00:23:24.720 --> 00:23:25.550
It's been a while.

00:23:25.550 --> 00:23:26.450
Have you been well?

00:23:26.450 --> 00:23:27.220
I've wanted to see you.

00:23:27.220 --> 00:23:28.120
How about you, Tatsuya?

00:23:28.120 --> 00:23:30.420
What about that girl? You're always together, right?

00:23:30.420 --> 00:23:33.560
And her eyes... When she looked at you, she seemed to be overlaying Dad's image onto you.

00:23:33.560 --> 00:23:34.490
You didn't notice?

00:23:34.490 --> 00:23:35.160
You're so dense.

00:23:35.160 --> 00:23:37.230
Tatsuya, little by little you've come to look just like Dad.

00:23:37.230 --> 00:23:39.300
That woman apparently knows Mom too.

00:23:39.300 --> 00:23:40.430
It'll be that way from now on too.

00:23:40.430 --> 00:23:42.500
Only a certain set of people will benefit from it.

00:23:42.500 --> 00:23:44.840
There's no way the expenses for childbirth could have been that much.

00:23:44.840 --> 00:23:47.500
I may not be much, but I still know just a little more about the world than you, Tatsuya.

00:23:47.500 --> 00:23:49.070
I'm more of an adult than before.

00:23:49.070 --> 00:23:50.870
Wasn't that day the same?

00:23:50.870 --> 00:23:54.000
That piano... I wonder if it's getting wet right now?
